      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-04T18:19:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the value assigned is exactly the same as what is generated by the compiler,\nit does not make any sense to add assignment, as it makes maintenance harder, e.g., if we want to add some value in the middle, we have to make a large change. \n\nI can remove the values from comment.",
      "parentUuid": "7eeb8edf_ece0cd93",
      "revId": "b1306d7a14928bc0e5d94a79d6b2419ddd08094b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0101c049_46bf4fc8",
        "filename": "system/stack/include/smp_api_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-04T18:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I want to review this change correctly, I have to go through the code and make sure this never gets cast to a different value.  I didn\u0027t check to see how hard that is, but at this stage, we should never add values in the middle.",
      "parentUuid": "b37791b6_373af90a",
      "revId": "b1306d7a14928bc0e5d94a79d6b2419ddd08094b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6fab240_e1bd947a",
